  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607198000: PostgreSQL pool observability, health and drain

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

Pool observability exposes only a fixed 32-byte counter record, never physical
channel identifiers, endpoints, credentials or mutable host state. Health
checks run `select 1` through each idle connection's compiled Kotoba provider;
failure closes and evicts that connection. Drain deadlines are fixed by host
configuration. Draining rejects every new acquire, permits existing leases to
finish and reset, and force-closes remaining connections at the deadline while
returning only the forced lease count.

Acquire must test pool status before attempting idle selection or growth. The
qualification exposed and fixed a race where the old expression could grow and
lease a connection before the later draining-status branch denied the call.

## Evidence

Released PostgreSQL qualification reads the fixed stats record, probes a healthy
connection, stalls a TLS proxy and observes health eviction and recovery. A
graceful drain rejects a concurrent acquire, waits for release/reset and returns
zero forced leases. A second drain crosses its host deadline, returns one and
invalidates the stale token. The full prior matrix and soak remain green.

This closes pool metrics, backpressure visibility, health eviction and graceful
or deadline-forced drain without widening guest authority."}]
